       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the labeled maximum for metformin, so I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as no more than 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. The ordered amount is about twice that daily maximum.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **850 mg three times daily** with meals, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1000 mg twice daily** with meals.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it as written. I'd add a note on the order that the dose is intentional and was verified with you."
      }
